msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid "Control types announcement"
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:187 src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:190
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid "Minimising to the system tray"
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:191
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid ""
"Elten does not have to occupy your taskbar all day. Press Tab to reach the che"
"ckbox. When it is ticked, minimising the Elten window sends it to the system t"
"ray instead, where the program keeps running quietly and continues to receive "
"notifications; the Elten icon in the tray brings the window back. Leave the op"
"tion unticked if you prefer Elten to behave like an ordinary window."
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:194
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid "Automatically minimise the Elten window to the system tray"
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:205
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid "Main window"
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:207
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid ""
"The main window is built of tabs: Notifications, the Feed and Quick Actions. N"
"ot everyone needs all three, so you can choose which of them are shown. The no"
"tifications tab has two habits of its own that you can adjust as well: by defa"
"ult it appears only while there are notifications to show, and you can decide "
"whether, and when, it takes focus as you return to the main window. All of thi"
"s can also be changed later under Tools, Program settings, Main window."
msgstr ""

#: src/scenes/welcome_wizard.rb:209
msgctxt "WelcomeWizard"
msgid ""
"In Elten 2.x, the main window had two tabs: Quick Actions and the feed. Elten "
"3.0 joins them with a third, Notifications, and leaves the whole arrangement t"
"o you: choose exactly the tabs you want to see. The notifications tab has two "
"habits of its own that you can adjust as well: by default it appears only whil"
"e there are notifications to show, and you can decide whether, and when, it ta"
"kes focus as you return to the main window. All of this can also be changed la"
"ter under Tools, Program settings, Main window."
msgstr ""

